        body: `A covered call means owning 100 shares of stock and simultaneously selling a call option against those shares. You receive premium immediately. If the stock stays below the strike at expiration, the option expires worthless and you keep the premium as additional income above any dividends received. If the stock rises above the strike, shares get called away at that price, capping your upside at the strike plus the premium received.

Covered calls are the safest options strategy because the cover, meaning owning the underlying shares, limits your loss to what a stock holder would experience. Monthly covered calls on moderately volatile stocks can generate 1 to 2 percent monthly premium income. The fundamental tradeoff is capping upside in exchange for immediate premium income.`,
