        body: `The Qualified Business Income (QBI) deduction allows eligible pass-through business owners to deduct up to 20% of qualified business income from their taxable income. For a sole proprietor with $200,000 in business income, the 20% QBI deduction reduces taxable income by $40,000, saving approximately $9,600 in taxes at the 24% marginal rate.

Limitations apply: specified service businesses (law, accounting, consulting, financial services, health) face income phase-outs beginning at $197,300 single ($394,600 married) in 2025. For businesses above these thresholds, the deduction phases out for service businesses and is capped at 50% of W-2 wages or 25% of wages plus 2.5% of qualified property for other businesses. This deduction is scheduled to expire after 2025 unless Congress extends it.`,
