        body: `If you expect to owe at least $1,000 in federal income tax after withholding and credits, and your withholding and credits will cover less than 90% of your current year tax liability or 100% of your prior year tax liability, you are required to make quarterly estimated tax payments. The 100% prior year safe harbor rises to 110% for taxpayers whose prior year AGI exceeded $150,000.

The groups most commonly required to make estimated payments: self-employed individuals and independent contractors who have no employer withholding, investors with significant capital gains, real estate investors with rental income, retirees whose pension and investment income is not sufficiently withheld, and anyone who receives non-wage income without adequate withholding.`,
