        body: `Most business assets wear out or become obsolete over time. Depreciation allows deducting the cost of these assets over their useful life, matching the expense with the period the asset generates revenue. Rather than deducting a $50,000 machine entirely in the year purchased, you deduct a portion annually for several years as the machine generates revenue.

The IRS's Modified Accelerated Cost Recovery System (MACRS) assigns depreciation periods based on asset type: 5 years for computers and cars, 7 years for office furniture and equipment, 27.5 years for residential rental property, 39 years for commercial real estate. MACRS accelerates deductions toward earlier years, meaning larger deductions in the early years of an asset's life.`,
