        body: `Bonus depreciation allows immediately deducting a large percentage of qualifying asset costs in the year placed in service, rather than depreciating over several years. The bonus depreciation rate was 100% from 2017 through 2022, then began phasing down: 80% in 2023, 60% in 2024, 40% in 2025, 20% in 2026, and 0% after 2026 unless Congress acts. This creates urgency for businesses considering large equipment purchases.

Section 179 expensing allows immediately deducting up to $1,220,000 in qualifying equipment and software in 2024, with the benefit phasing out above $3,050,000 in purchases. Unlike bonus depreciation, Section 179 is limited to taxable income (cannot create a loss) and applies only to property used more than 50% for business purposes. The combination of bonus depreciation and Section 179 can effectively eliminate the tax cost of major equipment purchases in the year acquired.`,
