        body: `Federal student loans are offered directly by the US Department of Education and carry significant advantages over private loans: income-driven repayment plans, loan forgiveness programs, deferment and forbearance options, and fixed interest rates set by Congress. Understanding the different loan types before borrowing allows strategic choices that dramatically affect total cost.

Direct Subsidized Loans are available to undergraduate students with demonstrated financial need. The government pays the interest while you are enrolled at least half-time, during the six-month grace period after leaving school, and during deferment. This interest subsidy makes subsidized loans significantly cheaper than unsubsidized loans over the borrowing period.`,
