        body: `The debt avalanche method prioritizes paying off debts in order of highest interest rate first while making minimum payments on all others. Mathematically, this minimizes total interest paid and is the most cost-efficient path to debt freedom. On a $30,000 debt portfolio including a 24% credit card, a 15% personal loan, and a 6% car loan, paying off the 24% card first saves the most money overall.

The debt snowball method, popularized by Dave Ramsey, prioritizes smallest balance first regardless of interest rate. This approach produces faster early wins: eliminating a $500 medical bill quickly generates motivation and reduces the number of accounts being managed. Research supports the psychological benefits of snowball for people who struggle with debt payoff adherence.`,
