        body: `Bankruptcy is a federal legal process providing relief from overwhelming debt through discharge (elimination) or reorganization. The decision to file involves weighing the immediate relief of stopping collection actions and eliminating dischargeable debt against the seven- to ten-year impact on your credit report and the asset exposure during the process. For some, bankruptcy is genuinely the best financial path; for others, negotiated settlements or debt management plans are preferable.

The automatic stay is one of bankruptcy's most immediate benefits: upon filing, all collection actions, foreclosures, wage garnishments, lawsuits, and creditor contact must immediately stop. This provides breathing room to reorganize financial affairs regardless of which chapter is ultimately filed.`,
