        body: `Lenders evaluate borrower creditworthiness through a framework of five characteristics known as the five Cs: capacity, capital, collateral, conditions, and character. Understanding this framework from the lender's perspective helps borrowers present their applications most effectively.

Capacity measures your ability to repay: income, employment stability, debt-to-income ratio, and cash flow after existing obligations. Lenders verify income through pay stubs, tax returns, and bank statements. Self-employed borrowers face additional scrutiny because income is less predictable and more manipulable through business expense deductions. Lenders typically require two years of tax returns for self-employed applicants.`,
