        body: `Series I Savings Bonds pay a composite interest rate combining two components: a fixed rate set at purchase that remains for the life of the bond (30 years) and a variable inflation adjustment component (the I rate) that resets every May 1 and November 1 based on the prior six months of CPI-U data.

The composite formula is slightly more complex than simple addition: composite rate = fixed rate + (2 times the semiannual inflation rate) + (fixed rate times the semiannual inflation rate). At a fixed rate of 1.3% and semiannual inflation of 1.48%, the composite is approximately 4.28% annualized. The composite rate changes every six months based on your purchase date: if you buy in March, your rate resets in September and March.`,
